## Wiki

A unified wiki lives at `{{WIKI_PATH}}/` — it holds **both** ingested research and your own project knowledge (four-layer memory model):
- `research/` — external content (articles, papers, videos): `active, long-term, tooling, best-practices, implementation, skills, orchestration, interesting-docs`
- `project/` — what we build: `components, decisions, architecture, patterns, troubleshooting, best-practices`
- `sessions/` — per-persona episodic logs

For an orientation, read `{{LLM_WIKI_PATH}}/README.md`.

## Working with this project

- Ingest external references (articles, docs, papers): `/wiki-update <url>` ad-hoc, or `/wiki-cycle` for batched discover → ingest → lint → promote
- Durable project decisions/components are filed inline as you work, and `/wrap-up` catches the rest at session end
- Promote staged entries: `/wiki-promote --review`
- Search prior research + decisions/components: `/wiki-search "<query>"`

See `CLAUDE.md` for the full session rhythm and conventions.

